#!/usr/bin/env bash
# UserPromptSubmit hook: re-inject Jake's hard writing/draft rules each turn so they
# never scroll out of context. Output is appended to the model's context for the turn.
cat <<'JSON'
{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"UserPromptSubmit","additionalContext":"JAKE'S HARD WRITING/DRAFT RULES (always apply to outward-facing content + drafts; non-negotiable):\n1. COPY-PASTE DRAFTS: stage each in a scratchpad file named *draft* (e.g. scratchpad/<slug>.draft.md) so the lint hook checks it, THEN present it in chat wrapped in escaped \\### delimiter lines that render as VISIBLE literal ### lines, with ZERO markdown inside the block. Never bare ###, never code fences, never blockquotes.\n2. NO em-dashes anywhere in Jake's writing... use an informal ellipsis or recast the sentence.\n3. Ellipsis takes NO following space: write word...word, not word... word.\n4. NO fabricated stories/numbers/incidents AND no invented reasoning or inferences in Jake's outward-facing writing... every claim and logical step comes ONLY from Jake's grilled take or his notes.\n5. GRILL before drafting any outward-facing content (gate, then grill, then draft). Never draft a GO before grilling.\n6. After any engagement grill: MANDATORY harvest of 1-2 Bluesky atomics (or explicitly say none surfaced), AND surface + FILE blog/second-brain candidates... do not merely offer.\n7. Do tedious lookups/harvest myself... never offload findable retrieval onto Jake.\n8. Before sending any draft or saying done: run a VISIBLE pre-delivery checklist against these rules."}}
JSON
